{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/extension/src/panel/Panel.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:49:36.261062Z","id":"63d08ff16b9b8e3edb3c853d909eeecaf40915372b111ca392f1c7b2ce50b8cf","body":{"detail":"Panel.svelte computes sendTo as the chosen agent, else the first live one in the daemon's order (most recently active), which can be a connected person's agent. The shell no longer does this (web/shell/src/view/send-menu.ts ownTarget; Send opens the menu when only other people's agents are live), so the panel's one-press Send can still route the owner's thread to Sam's agent and make routing requests.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":62},"end":{"line":62},"content_hash":"68fce108a4c4886829b15ba47878a1edc9f62e3df031ec56fb810856b20cbaa8"},"suggested_fix":"Use ownTarget with the owner's public ID, and open the menu when it is null, as ShellSidebar does.","summary":"The extension panel's default Send target is the first live agent, whoever's","tags":["task:23","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/extension/src/panel/Panel.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T12:08:21.317640Z","id":"e0332baafa779013729ec733088dd945b70c998119dee44014a479977135c6d8","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"63d08ff16b9b8e3edb3c853d909eeecaf40915372b111ca392f1c7b2ce50b8cf","summary":"The panel also lost \"approves first\": it embeds the shell Sidebar (Panel.svelte:304), whose SendMenu now fetches the relative /api/artifacts/{aid}/approves-first (web/shell/src/ui/SendMenu.svelte:22) from the extension page origin, which never reaches the daemon (the panel talks to it through the service worker, web/extension/src/sw/api.ts). Before bb547990 the panel read approves_first from thread views. The menu there names persons but never says who approves first.","tags":["review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/extension/src/panel/Panel.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:18:44.665125Z","id":"7ad56af5c3d044b3e4bc43cccdbd80ab4978269886631443a5a955e268de7b6a","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"e0332baafa779013729ec733088dd945b70c998119dee44014a479977135c6d8","summary":"Left for plan Task 23 (the extension's panel): the panel's menu asks nothing of the daemon from its own origin; it should ask through the service worker, as the owner's browser, under the 'Only about their content' rule.","tags":["task:23","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/extension/src/panel/Panel.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T03:40:37.890157Z","id":"e6860efff2c0b507fac412486b40da3d1c7bb2e45e3b0cad19dac1cfb8ec0871","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:a3ae32de","summary":"The panel's Send goes to ownTarget(agents, the owner's public ID), opens the menu when only other people's agents are live, and names a chosen other person's agent with its person; Elsewhere's cards follow the same rule. The menu asks who approves first through the worker (`firsts` -> GET /api/artifacts/{aid}/approves-first with the extension credential; the gateway admits it for live pages, Rule::Live). On a live page the answer is always [] in practice: a person's agents never see live pages (spec 2026-10-08 section 18, L10) and only the owner and its agents author there. Evidence: Panel.test.ts 'send menu names agents...', 'opens the menu rather than sending when only other people's agents are live', 'sends another page's thread to the owner's own agent there...'; sw/panel.test.ts 'asks the daemon who approves first...'; api_gateway::the_extension_acts_as_the_owner_on_live_pages and everything_else_is_refused; e2e chrome-overlay 'the panel's Send names the owner's agents, asks who approves first through the worker...' (200, {approves_first: []} from the extension origin) all pass.","supersedes":"63d08ff16b9b8e3edb3c853d909eeecaf40915372b111ca392f1c7b2ce50b8cf","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/extension/src/panel/link.svelte.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T03:49:30.467996Z","id":"89d4a6d682e845a7b3dca8d314ded60873591310c386bbb710787d9281ba40c3","body":{"detail":"Changing the return to `a?.t === \"far-page\" ? [] : null` leaves all 421 extension unit tests passing (vitest run extension). Panel.test.ts stubs link.firsts; link.test.ts covers clip and farPage (lines 107-135) but not firsts; the e2e in web/e2e/chrome-overlay.spec.ts:1136-1141 fetches approves-first from the service worker itself rather than through the panel's menu, and on a live page the answer is always [] (spec L10), so the hint could not show either way.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":219},"end":{"line":224},"content_hash":"eee93a717ebb36bd1893174a079af92598f1dd5fbf4cbc4a2cbf8b66ccc6ee1f"},"suggested_fix":"Add a link.test.ts case like farPage's: firsts posts {t: 'firsts', req, threadIds}, takes a valid answer, drops one with a non-public ID, and answers null on a lost worker.","summary":"PanelLink.firsts, the panel's real path to who-approves-first, has no test: a broken lookup passes every unit and the extension e2e","tags":["review","test","task:23","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/extension/src/panel/link.svelte.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T04:05:29.984025Z","id":"c60d4e165bb4ca46613904f8b770193ff1a8ffb1f5ee3d18d53655493b303939","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:21d2a440","summary":"link.test.ts 'asks the worker who approves first, and takes its answer, or none on a failure or a lost worker' checks the message PanelLink.firsts posts and the answer it returns, so a broken firsts fails it; passes.","supersedes":"89d4a6d682e845a7b3dca8d314ded60873591310c386bbb710787d9281ba40c3","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/extension/src/panel/link.svelte.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:58:44.761476Z","id":"dc92741d6dd998336640f63ed18d2d1853ab5c4e7bad1d0b7af04c3d17026abd","body":{"detail":"Every panel Chrome shows is the per-tab one the worker sets with `path: panelPath(tabId)` = `sidepanel.html?tab=<id>` (web/extension/src/sw/background.ts:30, 76); the global panel is disabled (background.ts:46). So `pinned` is always set and the `onActivated`/`onUpdated` listeners and `follow()`'s active-tab query (link.svelte.ts:75-78, 86-89, 154-158) never run. The comment at lines 81-83 says the unpinned form is for a browser test that opens the panel's page in a tab of its own, but the worker disconnects any `panel:` port whose sender has a tab (background.ts:245, `s.tab === undefined`), and web/e2e/chrome-overlay.spec.ts:117 drives the real side-panel target instead. A reader changing the panel's tab tracking has to work out which of the two paths is live.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":80},"end":{"line":93},"content_hash":"2ba42b9899b12081dd9feef38232592c394d28bd2c738e73371f99b40229a7f8"},"suggested_fix":"Remove the unpinned branch (the listeners, `onActivated`, `onUpdated`, and the active-tab query in `follow`) or, if a non-pinned panel is still wanted, say where it comes from; fix the comment at lines 81-83 and the file header's \"the state of the window's active tab\" to describe the pinned panel.","summary":"The side panel's follow-the-active-tab branch is unreachable in the shipped extension, and its comment says a browser test opens the panel in a tab, which the worker refuses","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/extension/src/panel/link.svelte.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:01:16.140504Z","id":"78817d385447b0fd4725f708b8ba04c9a71db63209925fa6a93013c563dba732","body":{"detail":"web/extension/src/sw/background.ts:30 panelPath = `sidepanel.html?tab=${tabId}`, line 76 showPanel sets that path per tab, line 46 disables the global panel; no manifest side_panel default_path exists (grep for side_panel in web/extension and web/scripts finds nothing). background.ts:245 admits a panel: port only when `s.tab === undefined`, so a panel page opened in a tab is disconnected, contradicting link.svelte.ts:81-83. web/e2e/chrome-overlay.spec.ts:117 attaches to the real side panel target. Kind suggestion fits.","kind":"comment","references":"dc92741d6dd998336640f63ed18d2d1853ab5c4e7bad1d0b7af04c3d17026abd","summary":"confirmed: every shipped panel carries ?tab=, so the unpinned follow-active-tab path is dead and its comment is wrong","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/extension/src/panel/InboxTab.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T17:05:25.579782Z","id":"452f87a85dc131ddd01188d611e33cebbc480f2eff46e0f5a30c0cc4fc3fb05a","body":{"detail":"/inbox groups unread and read items by artifact (web/shell/src/q/InboxPage.svelte with InboxGroup.svelte and inbox-groups.ts, over GET /api/inbox?group=artifact). The panel reaches the daemon only through the worker's typed messages (web/extension/src/messages.ts: inbox-page, inbox-mark-all), so grouping it needs a new inbox-groups request and answer with their validators and tests, the worker's handler, and the panel's paging per group; InboxGroup.svelte itself is reusable as is. Deferred to keep this change to the shell.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":20},"content_hash":"0bf9425c7a78e211f10400e1bac5224094b7f534faa22715670de6a9898fa4a8"},"suggested_fix":"Add an inbox-groups panel message carrying the filter, the group cursor and rows, answer it with the InboxGroupPage the shell's listInboxGroups returns, and render InboxGroup with InboxRow children in InboxTab.","summary":"The extension panel's Inbox tab still lists its items flat, not grouped by artifact","tags":["inbox","extension","status:deferred","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/extension/src/panel/link.svelte.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:04:32.616872Z","id":"7a5faba3d8818a8082f8db51bee5a3eea040676a0107e2514d26b23f9efb3077","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:5bc96e101","summary":"Fixed: the side panel watches only the tab its ?tab= names and drops the follow-the-active-tab path; web/extension link.test.ts \"watches its own tab\" and \"watches no tab when its page names none\" pass (//web:unit).","supersedes":"dc92741d6dd998336640f63ed18d2d1853ab5c4e7bad1d0b7af04c3d17026abd","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/extension/src/panel/Panel.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T23:17:45.840979Z","id":"c4a9b8a2d624b9e4608742b7e89d2d17891e1244902fadf06926877bd9da0ce9","body":{"detail":"The click handler (openInClax) asks the worker to open the page through the native host's login link; a middle-click or Cmd-click follows the anchor's own href, the daemon's plain address, which a browser profile with no session meets as the cold-browser page.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":375},"end":{"line":375},"content_hash":"b49dd6c4d91b66fc21ab8c9aeeca21b51f3a333fe9195bc67045efbf7d925478"},"summary":"Opening Open in Clax in a new tab by middle-click or a modifier skips the login link","tags":["extension","local-trust","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/extension/src/panel/Panel.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T23:31:03.564459Z","id":"309e77b85e1f03b09cfd6aa02d8eccda39d5f70a8cb28aa31af518e38c74f492","body":{"detail":"web/extension/src/panel/Panel.svelte renders Open in Clax as <button class=\"open\"> whose click posts open-clax (the worker opens the page through the native host's login link); it has no href. Evidence: bazelisk test //web:unit passes Panel.test.ts \"opens Open in Clax through the worker's login link, with no plain address to follow past it\" (no href, no link role, a click posts {t: \"open-clax\", path: \"/a/7q3k9mzx2b4t\"}); against the anchor of before 8f0c503e4 its getByRole(\"button\", {name: \"Open in Clax\"}) finds nothing.","kind":"resolve","ref":"git:8f0c503e4","summary":"Fixed: Open in Clax is a button, so no middle-click, modifier click or Open in new tab follows a plain address past the login link","supersedes":"c4a9b8a2d624b9e4608742b7e89d2d17891e1244902fadf06926877bd9da0ce9","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
